  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "An heirloom lace shawl is the most refined piece in the lacework collection. The body is a repeating column of seven-treble "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "shell-fan"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "shell fans"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " separated by "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "picot-arch"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "picot arches"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ". The border is six additional rows of increasing complexity, finishing with a deep scalloped "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "lace-border"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "lace border"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " along the lower triangle edge. Worked in lace weight on a 3.5 mm hook and fully "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "blocking"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "blocked"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ", the shawl reaches 180 cm wingspan and 85 cm deep at the "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "spine"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "spine"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "This is an advanced pattern. Each body row has multiple stitch types in a fixed sequence and the border chart requires reading a six-row repeat without losing position. Set aside uninterrupted time for the border rows."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "suppliesCard",
        "attrs": {
          "heading": "Materials",
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "Lace weight yarn",
              "qty": "500 g",
              "substitutions": "A fine merino or merino-silk lace weight takes blocking beautifully. Avoid very springy yarns as the fans compress back after pinning."
            },
            {
              "name": "3.5 mm crochet hook",
              "qty": "1"
            },
            {
              "name": "Tapestry needle",
              "qty": "1"
            },
            {
              "name": "Scissors",
              "qty": "1 pair"
            },
            {
              "name": "Blocking mats and T-pins",
              "qty": "1 set"
            },
            {
              "name": "Measuring tape",
              "qty": "1"
            },
            {
              "name": "Stitch markers",
              "qty": "6"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Gauge"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "1 shell fan (7 tr) + picot arch = 5 cm wide in lace weight with a 3.5 mm hook, blocked. Work one full body repeat swatch and block it before starting. The fan width determines the total wingspan at full stitch count. An unblocked fan is only 3.5 cm; blocking opens it to the full 5 cm."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Stitches used"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "bulletList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "ch: chain"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "sl st: slip stitch"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "dc (UK): double crochet"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "tr (UK): treble"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "dtr (UK): double treble, two yarn-overs before inserting hook"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                        "attrs": {
                          "termSlug": "shell-fan"
                        }
                      }
                    ],
                    "text": "Shell fan"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ": 7 tr into same space"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                        "attrs": {
                          "termSlug": "picot-arch"
                        }
                      }
                    ],
                    "text": "Picot arch"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ": ch 4, picot (ch 3, sl st into base ch), ch 4"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Foundation"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Ch 7. Work (3 tr, ch 3, 4 tr) into 7th ch from hook (first shell fan half at spine). Turn."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Body row: spine increase"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Ch 6. Work 1 dc into the 4th tr of the previous fan half. Work a "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "picot-arch"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "picot arch"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " (ch 4, ch 3 sl st to base, ch 4). Work 1 dc into the turning ch space. Work (3 tr, ch 3, 4 tr) into the ch-3 "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "spine"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "spine"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " space (spine increase fan). Work dc into turning ch of far side. Picot arch. Dc into 4th tr of the far fan half. Ch 6. 1 tr into the foundation base. Turn."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Pattern rows"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Each row grows by one shell fan on each side. The sequence for every row is: ch-6 edge arch, dc into far fan tr, picot arch, dc into ch-3 space between fans, *7-tr shell fan into dc position, dc into ch-3 space, picot arch, dc, picot arch, dc*, repeat to spine, spine fan (7 tr, ch 3, 7 tr), mirror back to right edge, ch-6 arch at right. Turn."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Continue working until the body measures 70 cm deep from the spine, measured straight down the centre back line. At this point work one plain dc row across the bottom edge to set the border start."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Six-row heirloom border"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Row B1: Dc across the full bottom edge, 1 dc per stitch and 2 dc into each chain space. Turn."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Row B2: Ch 5. *Skip 2 dc, 1 tr into next, ch 2*. Repeat across. Turn. (Open mesh row.)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Row B3: Sl st into first ch-2 space. *7 tr into next space (shell fan), ch 3, dc into next space, ch 3.* Repeat across. Turn. ("
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "shell-fan"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "Shell fan"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " row.)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Row B4: Dc into first tr. *Ch 3, picot (ch 3, sl st to base), ch 3, 1 dc into 4th tr of fan, ch 3, picot, ch 3, 1 dc into ch-3 arch.* Repeat across. Turn. ("
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "picot-arch"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "Picot arch"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " row.)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Row B5: Work one row of plain dc, placing 1 dc per stitch and 3 dc into each picot loop. Turn."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Row B6 (final "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "lace-border"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "lace border"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "): Ch 1. *1 dc into dc, ch 3, picot, ch 3, skip 2 dc.* Repeat across. Fasten off."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Blocking"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Soak the shawl for 30 minutes, press out excess water in a towel, and pin aggressively. Pin each border scallop point separately using T-pins. Pin the wingspan corners first to 180 cm apart, then the centre spine point to 85 cm. Fill all border scallops between. Leave 24 hours to dry. "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "blocking"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "Blocking"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " transforms the shawl: every shell fan opens, every picot stands clear, and the border scallops sharp."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "attrs": {
          "heading": "Common problems",
          "intro": "Heirloom lace shawls have exacting standards and specific failure points.",
          "items": [
            {
              "symptom": "Shell fans collapsing",
              "cause": "Not working into the correct dc between fans",
              "fix": "The 7-tr fan must go into a single dc stitch, not into a chain space. Mark every dc position with a removable marker before working the fan row."
            },
            {
              "symptom": "Picot arches uneven in size",
              "cause": "Inconsistent chain tension on the ch-4 on either side of the picot",
              "fix": "Work all ch-4 arches over a size 4 knitting needle and remove it before the next stitch. Consistent chain size is critical to even scallops in the border."
            },
            {
              "symptom": "Border pulling the shawl",
              "cause": "Border worked too tight against the body",
              "fix": "Work the dc pick-up row (B1) on a hook one size larger. A loose pick-up row is the foundation for the border and must not compress the body edge."
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    ]
  }
}